{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs36 Mass & Damping Measurement\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The Mass & Damping Compensation feature will automatically calculate the Velocity and Acceleration tuning parameters which reduce following error during the move in order to achieve quicker move step and settle times.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab To use this feature Select: Auto-Detect ...\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab Enter the Measurement Position\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab The Start Characterization button will move the stage to the measurement position, then move back and forth at the measurment position specified.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 4.\tx360\tab Values for the Payload added to the stage, Total Moving Mass, Kvff, and Kaff values will be calculated.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 5.\tx360\tab To Move the measured values to the values being used by the controller choose the Accept Results button\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 6.\tx360\tab The Kvff and Kaff can also be adjusted manually for fine tuning.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 7.\tx360\tab Choose the blue Apply button for the settings to take effect\sa180\par}
